## Two real defects my own tests caught mid-work (worth recording)

- `DossierEntry.decision_case_id.in_([case_id, None])` silently dropped EVERY
  subject-wide fact: SQL `col IN (x, NULL)` never matches a NULL row. Fixed to an
  explicit `or_(... == case_id, ... .is_(None))`. Without the subject-scope test
  this would have shipped as a snapshot that quietly ignored half the dossier.
- `recover_stale_runs()` returned **71 runs** on its first real call: the shared
  dev database is full of runs left mid-stage by earlier sessions. That is
  evidence the recovery gap was real, and also why the recovery test asserts
  against its own run id instead of global emptiness.

